## Run it

```bash
uv sync --locked                                  # exact dependencies, no resolution
uv run scenario scenario={{ scenario_id }} map={{ map_group }}
```

`--locked` is deliberate: if `uv.lock` and `pyproject.toml` ever disagree, the
command fails instead of quietly resolving something new. That is what makes
this directory reproducible.

The CARLA client is installed by this package, through the framework's
`{{ carla_extra }}` extra -- nothing has to be installed by hand.
{% if vendored_wheels %}
That client is published to no index, so its wheel travels in
[`{{ vendored_wheels }}/`]({{ vendored_wheels }}) and `pyproject.toml` points uv
at it with a relative `find-links`.
{% else %}
That client comes from an index, so nothing is vendored here.
{% endif %}

## Test it

```bash
uv run pytest
```

The bundled tests load, validate and compile the document. They need no CARLA
server, so they work as a smoke test anywhere.

## Ship it

```bash
pip install --no-index --find-links <wheelhouse> {{ distribution_name }}
scenario scenario={{ scenario_id }} map={{ map_group }}
```

A wheelhouse is this package's whole locked dependency graph, already built into
wheels. Installing from one needs pip and nothing else -- no `uv`, no `git`, no
network -- which is what lets a scenario be installed by Autoware's scenario
bridge, whose environment is a plain `python3-venv` with `python3-pip` in it.

The document and the Hydra config live *inside* `src/{{ package_name }}/`
precisely so that they are in the wheel: an installed scenario carries its own
scenario rather than needing this directory kept beside it.

## Layout

```
{{ package_name }}/
|-- pyproject.toml              # dependencies, pinned exactly
|-- uv.lock                     # the resolved dependency graph (commit this)
|-- .python-version             # {{ python_version }}
{% if vendored_wheels %}
|-- {{ vendored_wheels }}/
|   `-- carla-*.whl             # the client, vendored: not on any index
{% endif %}
|-- scenario/
|   `-- manifest.yaml           # what this package was generated from
|-- src/{{ package_name }}/
|   |-- __init__.py             # register() -- the entry point target
|   |-- scenario.py             # binds the document to DeclarativeScenario
|   |-- document.yaml           # the Scenario IR -- edit this
|   `-- conf/
|       `-- scenario/{{ scenario_id }}.yaml   # Hydra config for this scenario
`-- tests/
    `-- test_scenario.py
```

